comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T05:05:19.218Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,"CI diagnosis: named failure is an intentional coverage-gate fixture, not the failing suite. Real gate: branches 99.94 percent, index.ts line 2632. GH-1665 folds max-events onto maxEvents, making the kebab-key branch unreachable. Remove the obsolete alias branch; retain raw non-string and invalid-range handler validation. Add direct spelling-conflict host refusal with exit 2 and no boundary/output writes. This supersedes the separate earlier 1104 migration, which addressed literal SDK fixture fields."
  "2026-11-14T05:09:25.152Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,The reporting-window file passed 40/40 before removing the unreachable alias branch; the linked focused command also passes after removal and preserves non-git operation and typed refusals. This is dead-branch removal with unchanged handler behavior; reverting restores the demonstrated CI branch-coverage miss rather than a behavioral difference. Full release gates remain to run at 100 percent in every dimension.
  "2026-11-14T06:21:45.133Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,"| Failure | Cause (changelog) | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| coverage branches 99.94 percent; index.ts alias fallback | pm-cli 2026.11.8 GH-1665 maps max-events to maxEvents; named failure is a deliberate coverage fixture | delete unreachable kebab-key fallback; retain typed handler guards; prove spelling-conflict host code/exit 2 and no boundary/output writes |\n\nFocused reporting-window file passes 40/40. Typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings, canonical-reader acceptance, production audit, pack dry-run, release date, publish attestation and changelog checks pass. Both npm run release:check and bun run release:check complete 363 tests: 361 pass, two fail, zero skipped/canceled. The only failures are the two packed matrices reaching the unchanged 290-second outer deadline (null status), the class already tracked by pm-slack-standup-packed-timing. In both diagnostic reports the touched index.ts is 100 percent in all four dimensions; global diagnostic coverage is statements/lines 96.21, branches 99.88, functions 97.63 because accept-packed.ts is incomplete. Full unchanged coverage and packed certification remain required in CI. Neither deadlines, seed counts, source scope nor thresholds changed. Reverting the removed alias-key branch restores the baseline coverage miss without a behavioral difference; focused tests pass before and after."
